# Accessibility

Every interactive element is reachable, labelled, correctly typed and at least 44x44 points.

- Set `accessibilityRole` (valid values only: `react-native-a11y/has-valid-accessibility-role`), `accessibilityLabel` (a prop or derived from visible text), and `accessibilityState` for `disabled`, `selected`, `checked`, `busy` and `expanded` (`has-valid-accessibility-state`). Custom actions must be valid (`has-valid-accessibility-actions`).
- No touchable inside another touchable (`react-native-a11y/no-nested-touchables`).
- Touch targets are at least 44x44: add `hitSlop` where the visible element is smaller.
- `IconButton` requires `accessibilityLabel`. Inputs show errors with `accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"`.
- A loading `Button` sets `accessibilityState.busy`.
- Labels come from i18n, never literals (see `i18n.md`).
- RTL-safe layouts: `start` / `end`, never `left` / `right`; chevrons flip with direction.
- Respect `useReducedMotion` for animations. Text must scale up to `maxFontSizeMultiplier = 1.5`; do not disable scaling.
- Colors must keep contrast in light and dark themes; use theme tokens (`onPrimary` on `primary`, etc.).
- Give every shared component a `testID` prop and pass it down; inner parts get suffixes (`${testID}.label`).
- Tests assert role and state with `getByRole` (see `testing.md`).

```tsx
// ✅
<Pressable
  accessibilityRole="button"
  accessibilityLabel={t('actions.close', { ns: 'common' })}
  accessibilityState={{ disabled: isDisabled, busy: isLoading }}
  hitSlop={theme.spacing.md}
  testID={testID}
/>

// ❌ unlabelled icon-only touchable with a tiny target
<TouchableOpacity onPress={onClose}>
  <Icon name="close" size={16} />
</TouchableOpacity>
```
